From 5a66a9d09d110fa030c24503f63a328838dce9a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: video-pipeline-audit <fix@flexamarket.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 18:24:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix(video):=20root-cause=20repair=20of=20black-?=
 =?UTF-8?q?video=20bug=20(fl=5Ffaststart=20in=20delivery=20URL=20is=20inva?=
 =?UTF-8?q?lid=20=E2=86=92=20Cloudinary=20400)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Why
---
Cloudinary REJECTS every delivery URL containing the flag 'fl_faststart'
with HTTP 400 'Invalid flag in transformation: faststart'.  That HTTP 400
is what produces the persistent black-video / MediaError code 4 reports.

The codebase injected 'fl_faststart' into Cloudinary delivery URLs in 6
places, plus an admin migration endpoint that BACKFILLED the bad flag
across the entire database -- which is why every previously uploaded
boost video is broken in production today.

Evidence
--------
- The exact production URL for /listings/95 returns HTTP 400 (verified
  with curl).
- The same URL with fl_faststart removed returns HTTP 200 video/mp4
  codecs=avc1, accept-ranges bytes, CORS=*, range GET = 206.
- The same 400 is reproduced against Cloudinary's own demo cloud
  (fl_faststart against /demo/video/upload/), so this is platform
  behaviour, not per-cloud misconfiguration.
- ffprobe confirms the underlying upload is a valid H.264 / yuv420p MP4
  -- the asset is fine, only the URL transform was broken.

What this commit changes
------------------------
- lib/cloudinary.ts (backend): toStreamingUrl now strips stale
  fl_faststart segments (including the doubled form), collapses dup
  vc_h264 segments, applies vc_h264,f_mp4 exactly once, and is
  idempotent.  uploadVideoStream keeps the eager faststart flag (which
  IS valid at upload time) but routes the returned URL through
  toStreamingUrl.  prewarmVideo switched to a ranged GET (HEAD alone
  returns 423 without waiting).  IS_CONFIGURED now requires both
  CLOUDINARY_API_KEY and CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET.
- routes/listings.ts, routes/videos.ts: identical rewrite of local
  toStreamingVideoUrl.  listings.ts was missing the !includes guard,
  which is why DB rows have DUPLICATED fl_faststart segments.
- routes/admin.ts: the migrate-video-urls endpoint that originally
  *injected* fl_faststart is rewritten to *strip* it -- recovery, not
  destruction.  Idempotent.
- marketplace/src/lib/videoUrl.ts (frontend): full rewrite of
  toStreamingVideoUrl / toFetchableVideoUrl / toVideoPosterUrl with
  the same safe logic and a strongly-worded bug-history comment so
  this regression cannot be re-introduced.
- components/BoostWizard.tsx: warm URL builder now strips fl_faststart
  before issuing a ranged GET.
- scripts/repair-video-urls.sql: stand-alone, idempotent SQL migration
  for boost_video_url and listing_video_url columns.
- lib/__tests__/cloudinary.test.ts: 8 unit tests covering raw, single,
  doubled, idempotent, non-Cloudinary, image, empty, and the EXACT
  broken URL from production listing 95.  All passing (verified with
  tsx).

Test-evidence
-------------
test-evidence/AUDIT-REPORT.md contains the full audit, HTTP probes,
codec analysis, browser playback evidence, and rollout plan.
test-evidence/01-04 HTML files reproduce broken vs fixed playback.

Does NOT touch
--------------
nginx config, env vars, dependencies, package.json, DB schema,
Cloudinary cloud config.  Diff is intentionally minimal.
