+---
+
+## 7. Why every prior attempt failed
+
+Past investigations (yours and previous AI tools') focused on iPhone HEVC handling, Cloudinary configuration, faststart, moov-atom position, and CORS. All of those guesses were plausible — but each fix added MORE `fl_faststart` to URLs (because the public Cloudinary docs and many tutorials say to use it). The actual platform behaviour today is that **`fl_faststart` is only accepted inside an `eager: [{ flags: "faststart" }]` upload parameter; using it in a delivery URL is rejected with HTTP 400**. The codebase contained six places that wrote it into delivery URLs and an admin endpoint that backfilled it across the entire database. Until those were removed, no amount of cloud / NGINX / iPhone work could fix the symptom.
+
+I confirmed this with two independent live curls — against the user's Cloudinary cloud AND against Cloudinary's own demo cloud — both return identical `HTTP 400, x-cld-error: Invalid flag in transformation: faststart`. That's hard, reproducible, third-party-platform evidence.
+
+---
+
